stdout Circuit: end-to-end cpu write -> j211/j113 ribbon -> u9 74hct240 -> 74hct574 -> ipd90n10s4l06 with the real wpc timing and the active-low data (xspice digital latch). 6809e write cycle at 2 mhz: q rises at t0 = 10 us x k (one write per 10 us slot so that the 100 r / cgs gate rc settles), e rises t0 + 125 ns, e falls t0 + 375 ns; the asic strobe is low from q rise to e fall (370 ns as scoped on j211); cpu write data (u12 74ls240, enabled only for the write) is valid worst case from t0 + 200 ns (tddq max) to t0 + 405 ns (tdhw 30 ns min after e falls), tri-stated otherwise. ribbon 1 r / 120 pf, r318-r325 4.7 k pull-ups on the data, r310-r317 4.7 k on the strobes and blanking. register bit 1 -> ribbon low -> u9 high -> q high -> gate on. cycles: k=0 write 1, k=1 write 0, k=2 write 1, k=3 write 1 with the ribbon unplugged (no cpu, blanking floats up), k=4 write 1 with blanking high, k=5 write 0.
